# Mobile-First Design Standards

This is the design reference for Falak CRM. Every UI element MUST follow these
standards. The app is a PWA used primarily on phones and tablets — design for
touch first, then refine for desktop.

Sources: Apple HIG, Google Material Design 3, WCAG 2.2 (AA).

---

## 1. CSS Design Tokens

All sizing uses CSS custom properties defined in `globals.css`. These tokens
auto-adapt between touch devices (`pointer: coarse`) and desktop (`pointer: fine`).

**NEVER hardcode pixel sizes like `text-[11px]` or `w-6 h-6`.** Always use the
token-based classes or the CSS variables.

### How to use tokens in Tailwind

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — uses tokens, auto-adapts to device
<button className="text-body min-h-touch px-card">Save</button>
<p className="text-secondary">Subtitle</p>
<span className="text-label">LABEL</span>

// ❌ BAD — hardcoded, too small on mobile
<button className="text-[11px] px-2 py-1.5">Save</button>
<p className="text-[12px]">Subtitle</p>
<span className="text-[9px]">LABEL</span>
```

### Token reference

| Token | Mobile (touch) | Desktop (mouse) | Tailwind class |
|-------|---------------|-----------------|----------------|
| `--text-body` | 16px | 14px | `text-body` |
| `--text-secondary` | 14px | 12px | `text-secondary` |
| `--text-label` | 12px | 10px | `text-label` |
| `--text-button` | 14px | 12px | `text-button` |
| `--text-heading` | 20px | 18px | `text-heading` |
| `--text-subheading` | 16px | 14px | `text-subheading` |
| `--size-touch` | 44px | 32px | `min-h-touch` / `min-w-touch` |
| `--size-touch-lg` | 48px | 36px | `min-h-touch-lg` |
| `--size-icon-btn` | 40px | 28px | `w-icon-btn h-icon-btn` |
| `--size-icon-sm` | 18px | 14px | `w-icon-sm h-icon-sm` |
| `--size-icon-md` | 20px | 16px | `w-icon-md h-icon-md` |
| `--size-icon-lg` | 24px | 20px | `w-icon-lg h-icon-lg` |
| `--space-card` | 16px | 12px | `px-card` / `py-card` |
| `--space-card-sm` | 12px | 8px | `px-card-sm` / `py-card-sm` |
| `--space-section` | 24px | 16px | `gap-section` / `mb-section` |
| `--size-input` | 48px | 36px | `h-input` |
| `--size-list-item` | 48px | 36px | `min-h-list-item` |

