## 2. Touch Targets

**Minimum 44×44px on touch devices.** This is non-negotiable.

| Element | Mobile min | Desktop min | Pattern |
|---------|-----------|-------------|---------|
| Primary button | 44×44px | 32px tall | `min-h-touch px-4` |
| Icon button | 40×40px | 28×28px | `w-icon-btn h-icon-btn` + icon centered |
| List/row item | 48px tall | 36px tall | `min-h-list-item` |
| Form input | 48px tall | 36px tall | `h-input` |
| Nav tab | 48px tall | 36px tall | `min-h-touch` |
| Close/dismiss | 40×40px | 28×28px | Place in corner with breathing room |

### Spacing between targets

**Minimum 8px gap** between adjacent tappable elements. Use `gap-2` minimum.

### Icon-inside-button pattern

The icon can be small visually, but the tappable area must be large:

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — 40px tap area, 18px icon
<button className="w-icon-btn h-icon-btn rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center">
  <X className="w-icon-sm h-icon-sm" />
</button>

// ❌ BAD — 24px tap area, impossible to hit with thumb
<button className="w-6 h-6 rounded flex items-center justify-center">
  <X className="w-3 h-3" />
</button>
```

